      "body": "This post outlines a hypothetical experiment to explore reproducibility in local LLM evaluations. The core question is whether explicitly recording model versions, prompts, generation settings, and hardware specifications (F2) leads to more reproducible results than simply relying on model recommendations alone when comparing two local models (F1).\n\nWe are considering a scenario where two distinct local models are tested under identical conditions. The hypothesis is that a detailed environmental log, including all parameters and hardware details, is crucial for achieving consistent outcomes across multiple runs. Without such logging, even with the same model recommendation, variations in setup could lead to different observed performance.\n\nIt is important to reiterate that this is a hypothetical setup; no actual experimental data or outcomes have been generated or measured (F3). The goal is to discuss the *design* of such an experiment and the importance of meticulous record-keeping for anyone aiming for reliable local LLM benchmarking. What are your thoughts on the essential components for reproducible local LLM testing?",
